silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_3#gate a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline.sections.04_type_as_kleisli_arrow.concrete_anchor_3#gate" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_3#gate silm:hasLongDescription "The Gate is The Node-or-Arrow Gate is the intermediate object in the type factorization: Witness_record -> Gate -> TypedLeg_record. Gate checks whether the witness names a TypedNode (olog box), a TypedArrow (olog morphism), or neither (bot, refusal). For Witness_record: Gate = TypedNode_record. For an untyped witness like photoRecord2023: Gate = bot, chain halts." .
